    "updated_at": "2022-05-02T14:17:51Z",
    "body": "Interestingly this piece of standalone code in the same container never fails. It's basically the same code from where the warning is being logged by starship <https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/f81fcfe6f8e33b814a1f0eed97e67288bcdc9231/src/modules/memory_usage.rs#L34-L40>\r\n\r\n```rust\r\nuse std::process;\r\nuse std::{thread, time};\r\n\r\nfn main() {\r\n    let ten_millis = time::Duration::from_millis(10);\r\n\r\n    for _x in 1..1000 {\r\n        let _system = match sys_info::mem_info() {\r\n            Ok(info) => println!(\"{:?}\", info),\r\n            Err(err) => {\r\n                println!(\"Unable to access memory usage information:\\n{}\", err);\r\n                process::exit(1);\r\n            }\r\n        };\r\n\r\n        thread::sleep(ten_millis);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
