    "updated_at": "2022-05-02T14:36:43Z",
    "body": "Hmm, that's curious. That suggests that something in starship's execution environment is causing the mem_info call to fail (which I suppose would be consistent with it only triggering some of the time).\r\n\r\nIf this were any other language, I would immediately suspect a race condition corrupting the buffer (leading to the accusation of invalid UTF-8), but we don't use unsafe in this part of the codebase, and `sys_info` barely uses it on Linux...\r\n\r\nIf you run `starship prompt` manually (with `memory_usage` enabled), does that show roughly the same frequency of failures? Is it possible that this somehow only happens when starship is triggered as part of the prompt-draw process?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
